\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang {\pntxtb \'a8}}\faauto\ls1\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Items preceded by an asterisk (*) represent definitions agreed to among publishers which do not appear on the CDS document but may be present on individual publishers\rquote  surveys. 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *Academic advisement: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Plan under which each student is assigned to a faculty 
member or a trained adviser, who, through regular meetings, helps the student plan and implement immediate and long-term academic and vocational goals.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Accelerated program: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Completion of a college program of study in fewer than the usual number of years, most often by attending summer sessions and carrying extra courses during the regular academic term}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 .
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Admitted student: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Applicant who is offered admission to a degree-granting program}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 at your institution.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par 
\par *Adult student services: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Admission assistance, suppo
rt, orientation, and other services expressly for adults who have started college for the first time, or who are re-entering after a lapse of a few years.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 American Indian or Alaska native: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A person having origins in any of the original peoples of North America and who maintains cultural identification through tribal affiliation or community recognition.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Applicant (first-time, first year): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 An individual who has fulfilled the institution\rquote 
s requirements to be considered for admission (including payment or waiv
ing of the application fee, if any) and who has been notified of one of the following actions: admission, nonadmission, placement on waiting list, or application withdrawn (by applicant or institution).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Application fee: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 That amount of money that an institution charges for processing a student\rquote 
s application for acceptance. This amount is }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 not }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
creditable toward tuition and required fees, nor is it refundable if the student is not admitted to the institution.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Asian or Pacific Islander: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A person having origins i
n any of the original peoples of the Far East, Southeast Asia, the Indian Subcontinent, or {\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname place}}{\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname place}}Pacific{\*\xmlclose} {\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname place}}Islands{\*\xmlclose}
{\*\xmlclose}. This includes people from {\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname place}}China{\*\xmlclose}, {\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname place}}Japan{\*\xmlclose}, {\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname place}}Korea{\*\xmlclose}, the Philippine Islands, 
{\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname place}}American Samoa{\*\xmlclose}, {\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname place}}India{\*\xmlclose}, and {\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname place}}{\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname place}}Vietnam{\*\xmlclose}{\*\xmlclose}.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Associate degree: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
An award that normally requires at least two but less than four years of full-time equivalent college work.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Bachelor\rquote s degree: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
An award (baccalaureate or equivalent degree, as determined by the Secretary of the U.S. Department of Education) that normally requires at least four years but }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 not}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624  more than five years of full-time equivalent college-level work. This includes ALL bachelor\rquote s degrees conferred in a five-year cooperative (work-study plan) program. (A cooperative plan provide
s for alternate class attendance and employment in business, industry, or government; thus, it allows students to combine actual work experience with their college studies.) Also, it includes bachelor\rquote 
s degrees in which the normal four years of work are completed in three years.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Black, non-Hispanic: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A person having origins in any of the black racial groups of {\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname 
place}}Africa{\*\xmlclose} (except those of Hispanic origin).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Board (charges): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Assume average cost for 19 meals per week or the maximum meal plan.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Books and supplies (costs): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Average cost of books and supplies. Do not include unusual costs for special groups of students (e.g., engineering or art majors), unless they constitute the majority of students at your institution.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Calendar system: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 The method by which an institution structures most of its courses for the academic year.}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12546533 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\lang9\langfe1033\highlight7\langnp9\insrsid12546533\charrsid15677885 Campus Ministry:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\lang9\langfe1033\highlight7\langnp9\insrsid12546533\charrsid15677885  Religious student organizations (denominational or nondenominational) devoted to fostering religious life on college campuses. May also refer to Campu
s Crusade for Christ, an interdenominational Christian organization.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid12546533 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid12546533\charrsid12546533 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *Career and placement services: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
A range of services, including (often) the following: coordination of visits of employers to campus; aptitude and vocational testing; interest inventories, personal counseling; help in resume writing, interviewing, launching the job search; listings for t
hose students desiring employment and those seeking permanent positions; establishment of a permanent reference folder; career resource materials.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Carnegie units: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
One year of study or the equivalent in a secondary school subject.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Certificate: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 See }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Postsecond
ary award, certificate, or diploma.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Class rank: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
The relative numerical position of a student in his or her graduating class, calculated by the high school on the basis of grade-point average, whether weighted or unweighted.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 College-preparatory program: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Cou
rses in academic subjects (English, history and social studies, foreign languages, mathematics, science, and the arts) that stress preparation for college or university study. 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Common Application: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 The standard application form distributed by the National A
ssociation of Secondary School Principals for a large number of private colleges who are members of the Common Application Group. 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *Community service program: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Referral center for students wishing to perform volunteer work in the community or participate in volunteer activities coordinated by academic departments.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Commuter: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
A student who lives off campus in housing that is not owned by, operated by, or affiliated with the college. This category includes students who commute from home and students who have moved to the area to attend college. 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Contact hour: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
A unit of measure that represents an hour of scheduled instruction given to students. Also referred to as clock hour.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Continuous basis (for program enrollment): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A calendar system classification that is used
 by institutions that enroll students at any time during the academic year. For example, a cosmetology school or a word processing school might allow students to enroll and begin studies at various times, with no requirement that classes begin on a certai
n date.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid3695584 Cooperative }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid16467722\charrsid3695584 education}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid3695584  program: }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid3695584 A program that provides for alternate class attendance and }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid6951142\charrsid3695584 employment in business, industry, or government.}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid5328944\charrsid15034624 Cooperative housing: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid5328944\charrsid15034624 College-owned, -operated, or -affiliated housing in which students share room and board e
xpenses and participate in household chores to reduce living expenses.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *Counseling service: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Activities designed to assist students in making plans and decisions related to their education, career, or personal development.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Credit: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Recognition of attendance or performance in an instructional activity (course or program) that can be applied by a recipient toward the requirements for a degree, diploma, certificate, or other formal award.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Credit course: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A course that, if successfully co
mpleted, can be applied toward the number of courses required for achieving a degree, diploma, certificate, or other formal award.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Credit hour: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
A unit of measure representing an hour (50 minutes) of instruction over a 15-week period in a semester or trimes
ter system or a 10-week period in a quarter system. It is applied toward the total number of hours needed for completing the requirements of a degree, diploma, certificate, or other formal award.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Cross-registration: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A system whereby students enrolled at on
e institution may take courses at another institution without having to apply to the second institution.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par Deferred admission: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 The practice of permitting admitted students to postpone enrollment, usually for a period of one academic term or one year.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Degree: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
An award conferred by a college, university, or other postsecondary education institution as official recognition for the successful completion of a program of studies.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Degree-seeking students: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Students enrolled in courses for credit who are recognized by
 the institution as seeking a degree or formal award. At the undergraduate level, this is intended to include students enrolled in vocational or occupational programs.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Differs by program (calendar system): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A calendar system classification that is used by i
nstitutions that have occupational/vocational programs of varying length. These schools may enroll students at specific times depending on the program desired. For example, a school might offer a two-month program in January, March, May, September, and No
vember; and a three-month program in January, April, and October.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Diploma: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 See }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Postsecondary award, certificate, or diploma.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Distance learning: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
An option for earning course credit at off-campus locations via cable television, internet, satellite classes, videotapes, correspondence courses, or other means.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Doctoral degree: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
The highest award a student can earn for graduate study. The doctoral degree classification includes such degrees as Doctor of Education, Doctor of Juridical Science, Doctor of Public Healt
h, and the Doctor of Philosophy degree in any field such as agronomy, food technology, education, engineering, public administration, ophthalmology, or radiology. For the Doctor of Public Health degree, the prior degree is generally earned in the closely 
related field of medicine or in sanitary engineering.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Double major: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Program in which students may complete two undergraduate programs of study simultaneously.}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par Dual enrollment: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A program through which high school students may enroll in college courses while 
still enrolled in high school. Students are not required to apply for admission to the college in order to participate.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Early action plan: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
An admission plan that allows students to apply and be notified of an admission decision well in advance of the regular notification dates. If admitted, the candidate is not committed to enroll; the student may reply to the offer under the college\rquote 
s regular reply policy.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Early admission: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A policy u
nder which students who have not completed high school are admitted and enroll full time in college, usually after completion of their junior year.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Early decision plan: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A plan that permits students to apply and be notified of an admission decision (and fin
ancial aid offer if applicable) well in advance of the regular notification date. Applicants agree to accept an offer of admission and, if admitted, to withdraw their applications from other colleges. There are three possible decisions for early decision 
applicants: admitted, denied, or not admitted but forwarded for consideration with the regular applicant pool, without prejudice.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 English as a Second Language (ESL): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
A course of study designed specifically for students whose native language is not English.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Exchange student program-domestic: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Any arrangement between a student and a college that permits study for a semester or more at another college}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624  in the United States }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 without extending the amount of time required for a degree. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 See also Study abroad}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 .
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 External degree program:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
 A program of study in which students earn credits toward a degree through independent study, college courses, proficiency examinations, and personal experience. External degree programs require minimal or no classroom attendance.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Extracurricular activities (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Special consideration in the admissions process given for participation in both school and nonschool-related activities of interest to the college, such as clubs, hobbies, student government, athletics, performing arts, etc.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 First professional certificate (postdegree): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
An award that requires completion of an organized program of study designed for persons who have completed the first professional degree. Examples could be refresher courses or additional units of study in a specialty or subspecialty.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 First professional degree: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
An award in one of the following fields: Chiropractic (DC, DCM), dentistry (DDS, DMD), medicine (MD), optometry (OD), osteopathic medicine (DO), rabbinical and Talmudic studies (MHL, Rav), Pharma
cy (BPharm, PharmD), podiatry (PodD, DP, DPM), veterinary medicine (DVM), law (LLB, JD), divinity/ministry (BD, MDiv).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 First-time student: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
A student attending any institution for the first time at the level enrolled. Includes students enrolled in the fall 
term who attended a postsecondary institution for the first time at the same level in the prior summer term. Also includes students who entered with advanced standing (college credit earned before graduation from high school).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 First-time, first-year (freshman) student: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
A student attending any institution for the first time at the undergraduate level. Includes students enrolled in the fall term who attended college for the first time in the prior summer term. Also includes students who entered with advanced 
standing (college credits earned before graduation from high school).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 First-year student: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
A student who has completed less than the equivalent of 1 full year of undergraduate work; that is, less than 30 semester hours (in a 120-hour degree program) or less than 900 contact hours.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Freshman: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A first-year undergraduate student.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *Freshman/new student orientation: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Orientation addressing the academic, social, emotional, and intellectual issues involved in beginning college. May be a few hours or a few days in length; at some colleges, there is a fee.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Full-time student (undergraduate): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A student enrolled for 12 or more semester credits, 12 or more quarter credits, or 24 or more contact hours a week each term.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Geographical residence (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Special co
nsideration in the admission process given to students from a particular region, state, or country of residence.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Grade-point average (academic high school GPA): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
The sum of grade points a student has earned in secondary school divided by the number of cours
es taken. The most common system of assigning numbers to grades counts four points for an A, three points for a B, two points for a C, one point for a D, and no points for an E or F. Unweighted GPA\rquote 
s assign the same weight to each course. Weighting gives students additional points for their grades in advanced or honors courses.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Graduate student: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A student who holds a bachelor\rquote 
s or first professional degree, or equivalent, and is taking courses at the post-baccalaureate level.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *Health services: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Free or low c
ost on-campus primary and preventive health care available to students.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 High school diploma or recognized equivalent: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A document certifying the successful completion of a prescribed secondary school program of studies, or the attainment of satisfactory sco
res on the Tests of General Educational Development (GED), or another state-specified examination.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Hispanic: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
A person of Mexican, Puerto Rican, Cuban, Central or South American, or other Spanish culture or origin, regardless of race.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Honors program:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624  Any sp
ecial program for very able students offering the opportunity for educational enrichment, independent study, acceleration, or some combination of these.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624  
\par Independent study: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Academic work chosen or designed by the student with the approval of the department concerned, under an instructor\rquote 
s supervision, and usually undertaken outside of the regular classroom structure.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par In-state tuition: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 The tuition charged by institutions to those students who meet the state\rquote s or institution\rquote s residency requirements.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 International student: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 See}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
 Nonresident alien.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid593585 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\highlight7\insrsid12546533\charrsid10096671 International student group: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\highlight7\insrsid593585\charrsid593585 Student groups that facilitate cultural dialogue, support a diverse campus, assist international students in acclimation and creating a social network.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\cf2\insrsid593585 \~
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Internship:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
 Any short-term, supervised work experience usually related to a student\rquote s major field, for which the student earns academic credit. The work can be full- or part-time, on- or off-campus, paid or unpaid.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *Learning center: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Center offering assistance through tutors, workshops, computer programs, or audiovisual equipment in reading, writing, math, and skills such as taking notes, managing time, taking tests.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par *Legal services: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Free or low cost legal advice for a range of issues (personal and other).}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Liberal arts/career combination: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Program in which a student earns undergraduate degrees in two separate fields, one in a liberal arts major and the other in a professional or specialized major, whether on campus or through cross\_registration.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Master\rquote s degree: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
An award that requires the successful completion of a program of study of at least the full-time equivalent of one but not more than two academic years of work beyond the bachelor\rquote s degree.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Minority affiliation (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Special considerat
ion in the admission process for members of designated racial/ethnic minority groups.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *Minority student center: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Center with programs, activities, and/or services intended to enhance the college experience of students of color.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid12546533 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid12546533 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\lang9\langfe1033\highlight7\langnp9\insrsid12546533\charrsid475215 Model United Nations: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \lang9\langfe1033\highlight7\langnp9\insrsid12546533\charrsid475215 A simulation activity focusing on conflict resolution, globalization, and diplomacy. Assuming roles as foreign ambassadors and \'93delegates,\'94
 students conduct research, engage in debate, draft resolutions, and may participate in a national Model UN conference.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid12546533   
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Nonresident alien: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
A person who is not a citizen or national of the United States and who is in this country on a visa or temporary basis and does not have the right to remain indefinitely.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *On-campus day care: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Licensed day care for students\rquote  children (usually age 3 and up); usually for a fee.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Open admission: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Admission policy under which virtually all secondary school graduates or students with GED equivalency diplomas are admitted without regard to academic record, test scores, or other qualifications.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Other expenses (costs): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Include average costs for clothing, laundry, entertainment, medical (if not a required fee), and furnishings.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Out-of-state tuition: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 The tuition charged by institutions to those students who do not meet the institution
\rquote s or state\rquote s residency requirements.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Part-time student (undergraduate): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
A student enrolled for fewer than 12 credits per semester or quarter, or fewer than 24 contact hours a week each term.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *Personal counseling}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
: One-on-one or group counseling with trained professionals for students who want to explore personal, educational, or vocational issues.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Post-baccalaureate certificate: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 An award that requires completion of an organized program of study requiring 18 credit hours beyond the bachelor\rquote s; designed for persons who have com
pleted a baccalaureate degree but do not meet the requirements of academic degrees carrying the title of master.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Post-master\rquote s certificate: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
An award that requires completion of an organized program of study of 24 credit hours beyond the master\rquote s degree but does not meet the requirements of academic degrees at the doctoral level.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid14565466 Postsecondary award, certificate, or diploma: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid14565466 Includes the following three IPEDS definitions for postsecondary awards, certificates, and diplomas of varying durations and credit/contact hour requirements\emdash 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li360\ri324\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin324\lin360\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid14565466 Less Than 1 Academic Year:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid14565466  Requires completion of an organized program of study at the postsecondary level (below the baccalaureate degree) in less than 1 academic year (2 semesters or 3 quarters) or in less than 900 contact hours 
by a student enrolled full-time.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid14565466 At Least 1 But Less Than 2 Academic Years:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid14565466 
 Requires completion of an organized program of study at the postsecondary level (below the baccalaureate degree) in at least 1 but less than 2 full-time equivalent academic years, 
or designed for completion in at least 30 but less than 60 credit hours, or in at least 900 but less than 1,800 contact hours.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ai\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid14565466 At Least 2 But Less Than 4 Academic Years:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid14565466 
 Requires completion of an organized program of study at the postsecondary level (below
 the baccalaureate degree) in at least 2 but less than 4 full-time equivalent academic years, or designed for completion in at least 60 but less than 120 credit hours, or in at least 1,800 but less than 3,600 contact hours.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid1211867 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\highlight7\insrsid1211867 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Private institution: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 An educati
onal institution controlled by a private individual(s) or by a nongovernmental agency, usually supported primarily by other than public funds, and operated by other than publicly elected or appointed officials.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Private for-profit institution: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A private ins
titution in which the individual(s) or agency in control receives compensation, other than wages, rent, or other expenses for the assumption of risk.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par Private nonprofit institution: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A private institution in which the individual(s) or agency in control recei
ves no compensation, other than wages, rent, or other expenses for the assumption of risk. These include both independent nonprofit schools and those affiliated with a religious organization.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Proprietary institution: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 See}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
 Private for-profit institution.
\par Public institution: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
An educational institution whose programs and activities are operated by publicly elected or appointed school officials, and which is supported primarily by public funds.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Quarter calendar system: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A calendar system in which the academic yea
r consists of three sessions called quarters of about 12 weeks each. The range may be from {\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname place}}10{\*\xmlclose} to 15 weeks. There may be an additional quarter in the summer.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Race/ethnicity: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Category used to describe groups to which individuals belong, identify with, or belong in the eyes of the community. The categories do not denote scientific definitions of anthropological origins. A person may be counted in only one group.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Race/ethnicity unknown: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Category used to classify students or employees whose race/ethnicity is not known and whom institutions are unable to place in one of the specified racial/ethnic categories.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Religious affiliation/commitment (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Special considerat
ion given in the admission process for affiliation with a certain church or faith/religion, commitment to a religious vocation, or observance of certain religious tenets/lifestyle. 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *Religious counseling: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
One-on-one or group counseling with trained professionals for students who want to explore religious problems or issues.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *Remedial services: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Instructional courses designed for students deficient in the general competencies necessary for a regular postsecondary curriculum and educational setting.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Required fees: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Fixed sum charged to students for items not covered by tuition and required of such a large proportion of all students that the student who does NOT pay is the exception. Do not include application fees or optional fees such as lab fees or parking fees. 

\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Resident alien or other eligible non-citizen: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
A person who is not a citizen or national of the United States and who has been admitted as a legal immigrant for the purpose of obtaining permanent resident alien status (and who holds either an alien regi
stration card [Form I-551 or I-151], a Temporary Resident Card [Form I-688], or an Arrival-Departure Record [Form I-94] with a notation that conveys legal immigrant status, such as Section 207 Refugee, Section 208 Asylee, Conditional Entrant Parolee or Cu
ban-Haitian).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Room and board (charges)\emdash on campus: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Assume double occupancy in institutional housing and 19 meals per week (or maximum meal plan).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Secondary school record (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Information maintained by the secondary school that may include s
uch things as the student\rquote s high school transcript, class rank, GPA, and teacher and counselor recommendations.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Semester calendar system: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
A calendar system that consists of two semesters during the academic year with about 16 weeks for each semester of instruction. There may be an additional summer session.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Student-designed major: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
A program of study based on individual interests, designed with the assistance of an adviser.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Study abroad:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624  Any arrangement by which a student completes part of the college progra
m studying in another country. Can be at a campus abroad or through a cooperative agreement with some other {\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname place}}{\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname place}}U.S.{\*\xmlclose}{\*\xmlclose}
 college or an institution of another country.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *Summer session: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A summer session is shorter than a regular semester and not considered
 part of the academic year. It is not the third term of an institution operating on a trimester system or the fourth term of an institution operating on a quarter calendar system. The institution may have 2 or more sessions occurring in the summer months.
 Some schools, such as vocational and beauty schools, have year-round classes with no separate summer session.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Talent/ability (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Special consideration given to students with demonstrated talent/abilities in areas of interest to the institution (e.g., sports, the arts, languages, etc.).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Teacher certification program:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
 Program designed to prepare students to meet the requirements for certification as teachers in elementary, middle/junior high, and secondary schools.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Transfer applicant: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 An in
dividual who has fulfilled the institution\rquote s requirements to be considered for admission (including payment or waiving of the application fee, if any) and who has previously attended another college or university and earned college-level credit. 

\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par Transfer student:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
 A student entering the institution for the first time but known to have previously attended a postsecondary institution at the same level (e.g., undergraduate). The student may transfer with or without credit.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Transportation (costs): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Assume two round trips to student\rquote s hometown per year for students in institutional housing or daily travel to and from your institution for commuter students.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Trimester calendar system: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 An academic year consisting of 3 terms of about 15 weeks each.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Tuition: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Amount of
 money charged to students for instructional services. Tuition may be charged per term, per course, or per credit. 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par *Tutoring: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 May range from one-on-one tutoring in specific subjects to tutoring in an area such as math, reading, or writing. Most tutors ar
e college students; at some colleges, they are specially trained and certified.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Unit: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
a standard of measurement representing hours of academic instruction (e.g., semester credit, quarter credit, contact hour).
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Undergraduate: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
A student enrolled in a four- or five-year bachelor\rquote s degree program, an associate degree program, or a vocational or technical program below the baccalaureate.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *Veteran\rquote s counseling: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Helps veterans and their dependents obtain benefits for their selected program and provides certifications to the Veteran\rquote s Administration. May also provide personal counseling on the transition from the military to a civilian life.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *Visually impaired: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Any person whose sight loss is not correctable and is sufficiently severe as to adversely affect educational performance.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Volunteer work (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Special consideration given to students for activity done on a volunteer basis (e.g., tutoring, hospital care, working with the elderly or disabled) as a service to the community or the public in general.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Wait list: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 List of students who meet the admission 
requirements but will only be offered a place in the class if space becomes available. 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Weekend college:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
 A program that allows students to take a complete course of study and attend classes only on weekends. 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 White, non-Hispanic: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 A person having origins in any of the original peoples of Europe, North Africa, or the 
{\*\xmlopen\xmlns2{\factoidname place}}Middle East{\*\xmlclose} (except those of Hispanic origin).
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 *Women\rquote s center: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
Center with programs, academic activities, and/or services intended to promote an understanding of the evolving roles of women.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sb120\sa120\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Work experience (as admission factor): }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Special consideration given to students who have been employed prior to application, whether for relevance to major, demonstration of employment-related skills, or as explanation of student\rquote 
s academic and extracurricular record.
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 \page 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qc \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs24 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs24\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Financial Aid Definitions
\par 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3755021 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid3755021\charrsid3695584 External scholarships and grants: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid3755021\charrsid3695584 Scholarships and grants received from outside (private) sources that students bring with them (e.g., Kiwanis, National Merit scholarships). The institution may process paperwork 
to receive the dollars, but it has no role in determining the recipient or the dollar amount awarded.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid3755021\charrsid15034624 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid3755021 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Financial aid applicant: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Any applicant who submits }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 any one of}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624  the institutionally required financial aid applications/forms, such as the FAFSA. 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Indebtedness: }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 Aggregate dollar amount bo}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid1471844 
rrowed through any loan program}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 
 (federal, state, subsidized, unsubsidized, private, etc.; excluding parent loans) while the student was enrolled at an institution. Student loans co-signed by a parent are assumed to be the responsibility of the student and }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624 should}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid9600684\charrsid15034624  be included.
\par 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1471844 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid1471844\charrsid3695584 Institutional scholarships and grants}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\cf1\insrsid1471844\charrsid3695584 : Endowed scholarships, annual gifts and tuition funded grants for which the institution determines the recipient.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid1471844\charrsid15034624 
